{
  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) achieved 0.591 acc / 0.573 F1, a substantial +10.6 pt gain over config_001 (singleprofile, same encoder, 0.485 acc), confirming that multiprofile + aggregation is the most impactful design choice so far. Image-only resnet50 (config_010) is very weak (0.208), so multimodal fusion with resnet50 is not yet justified. Uncertainty: we do not yet know whether the aggregation method itself matters—i.e., whether a transformer aggregator can further improve over simple average pooling. This experiment (config_003) changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding model_setting, profile_setting, and encoder identical to config_002, giving a clean single-variable comparison. It is the best use of the next budget slot because it isolates the aggregation effect within the currently strongest modality, and the result will directly inform which aggregation to carry into all subsequent multimodal experiments (configs 018–051), reducing uncertainty across a large portion of the remaining search space."
}

